an class=\\\"strong\\\">can't have messed</span> this up.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"could have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"couldn't have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">couldn't have</span> left it on the table.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">may have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"may have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"may not have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">may have been</span> distracted.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">might have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"might have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"might have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might have gotten</span> lost.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">must have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must not have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">must have forgotten</span> about it.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ought to have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ought to have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ought not to have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> ought to have apologized</span> for making a mess.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">should have</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should not have + past participleught not to have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">shouldn't have been</span> so nice.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">would have</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"would have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"would not have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> wouldn't have told </span>him to go away.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">shouldn't have been</span> so controlling.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">must not have heard</span> a word I said yesterday. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">could have just let it go</span>, but nooooooo! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">ought to have listened</span> to me. You<span class=\"strong\"> can't have messed</span> this up!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't have bought</span> that line. I <span class=\"strong\">would have told </span>him to get lost.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Differences", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to make comparisons and identify contrasts in writing and in polite speech, you can use a number of phrases.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the words and phrases:<span class=\"strong\"> difference</span>, <span class=\"strong\">differ</span>, <span class=\"strong\">in contrast</span> and <span class=\"strong\">unlike</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">One important <span class=\"strong\">difference</span> is that women still make less money than men on average.</br><span class=\"strong\"> In contrast </span>to men, women still make less money on average.</br> The results of the research <span class=\"strong\">differ</span> from earlier studies. </br><span class=\"strong\">Unlike </span>other studies, this one didn't take inflation into account.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "One important <span class=\"strong\">difference</span> between Amy and other people is that Amy is very rational and level-headed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Unlike</span> some people I know.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">In contrast</span> to me, Bill moves rather fast. But, isn't this a form of workplace harassment?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The important<span class=\"strong\"> difference </span>is that we would be going together as friends.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Our opinion of Bill<span class=\"strong\"> differs</span> greatly.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "informers", "type": "name"}, {"content": "people who report on the activities of others, especially to authorities", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My informers told me you had a busy evening last night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when talking about a difficult situation.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "apprehensive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "anxious or fearful that something bad or unpleasant will happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You had to be an apprehensive little boy who got his feelings hurt. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "level-headed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "calm and sensible", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Amy is very rational and level-headed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "let cooler heads prevail", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to take a break from a frustrating situation, revisiting the subject once one is calm", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She is more than willing to let cooler heads prevail. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to escalate", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to become more intense", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That escalated quickly.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "harassment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "aggressive pressure or intimidation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: But, isn't this a form of workplace harassment?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With the class, brainstorm all the different types of reality TV.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, create a survey about the viewing habits of your classmates in relation to reality TV.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out which shows they prefer and which shows they dislike.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take notes explaining their opinions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your findings to the class.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use words of contrast to help make your presentation more descriptive.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm the different types of reality TV.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I collaborate with a partner and create a survey about the reality TV viewing habits of my classmates.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I take notes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my findings using contrastive vocabulary.", "type": "text"}]}]}